{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfryNmc2yFG9oqe7i9R2S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The migration is done and the tests pass (2 passed). I didn't commit anything.\n\n- **`config.toml`** (new): the same three sections and keys as before. `host`, `url` and `debug` are a string, a string and a boolean. `port`, `pool_size` and `max_upload_mb` are ints, `timeout` is a float, and `beta` is a boolean.\n- **`app/config.py`**: `load_config` now reads the file in binary mode and returns `tomllib.load(f)`. The result has the same `{section: {key: value}}` shape, now with real types. The default path changed from `config.ini` to `config.toml`.\n- **`config.ini`**: deleted.\n- **`tests/test_config.py`**: kept the existing section and host checks and added `test_value_types`, which asserts the int, float and bool types. This goes beyond the request, so say if you'd rather not have it.\n\nOne behavior change: a missing file used to return `{}` silently, because configparser ignores missing files. Now `load_config` raises `FileNotFoundError`. I think that's the better behavior, but it is a change if anything relies on the empty return.\n\nI removed the `__pycache__` directories my test run created so the tree only shows the intended changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10536,"cache_read_input_tokens":50204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10536},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70c7e6cb-b6a7-4d5c-ad84-ac524ec9b1b0","uuid":"69771ddd-30ab-4263-a5ff-9a99c91cb211","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:23:52.140Z","request_id":"req_011CfryNmKgQPP2XFZx9KtsU"}
